# The site's onion, as the web server compose's tor runs it (docs/two-machines.md): one onion
# service, its keys in /var/lib/tor (the host's /var/lib/ccs-tor, the tor account's), its port 80
# Caddy's socket (www). A single-hop service: the site is public and its address known, so the
# server's own anonymity buys nothing and three hops fewer make it quicker. No SOCKS port (a
# single-hop service may not have one), no relaying (built without it).
SocksPort 0
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor/data
HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/ccs
HiddenServicePort 80 unix:/run/ccs-www/onion.sock
HiddenServiceNonAnonymousMode 1
HiddenServiceSingleHopMode 1
Log notice stdout
